  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><ul> <li>Identify the longest carbon chain containing the functional group: The longest carbon chain is four carbons long, indicating the prefix \"butan-\".</li> <li>Number the carbons in the chain: Begin numbering from the end nearest to the functional group. </li> <li>Identify and name substituent groups: The amino group (–<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>) is present as a substituent on carbon number 3. It is named as \"amino\".</li> <li>Identify the functional group: The functional group present is the nitrile group (–CN).</li></ul><p>Combining all parts, the IUPAC name \"3-Aminobutanenitrile\" is derived.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0121_9192d3bc9ffd.png\" style=\"width: 450px; height: 247px;\"/></p><p>Hence, the answer is option C.</p></blockquote>"
